or the rest of the season’s scheduled payments. The Monthly Base Fee is the Seasonal Rate divided by the number of monthly periods in the season. For example, a $3,000 season with 6 monthly periods has a $500 base fee, so $250 would be forfeited. | Changes and Other Rules | Any change made before the deadline, including a partial cancellation, is subject to a", "on. For example, a $3,000 season with 6 monthly periods has a $500 base fee, so $250 would be forfeited. | Changes and Other Rules | Any change made before the deadline, including a partial cancellation, is subject to a $10 fee. Changes made after the deadline forfeit the deposit, and you may become responsible for the full contracted amount. Credit card convenience fees are never refundable. | All cancellations must"], "via": "View Park"}]}
